# MadGraph5 batch script: u u~ > c c~ e+ e- mu+ mu- at LO, QCD=0
# Single-flavor, single-subprocess version of pp_to_qq4l for HELAS amplitude validation.
#
# Why this exact process:
#   - Different-flavor quark lines (u vs c) + diagonal CKM => only the s-channel
#     EW connection between the two quark lines => a single color flow (NCOLOR=1).
#     This is reproducible by vibegraph's coherent diagram sum without color-flow code.
#   - Distinct leptons (e, mu) => no identical final-state particles, so MadGraph's
#     IDEN is pure spin*color averaging (4*9=36) with no symmetry factor.
#   - One concrete subprocess => the matrix element is matrix1 (no matrix9 to extract).
#
# This is a MadEvent output (default), so `launch` also yields the total cross
# section for a future validate-vegas reference.
generate u u~ > c c~ e+ e- mu+ mu- QCD=0
output uux_to_ccx_emmm_qcd0 -nojpeg
# launch compiles the process (producing the helicity-recycled matrix1_optim.f
# for the optimized-routine timing comparison) and integrates the cross section
# (a future validate-vegas reference).  lpp=0 => no PDF: fixed-energy partonic
# beams (u, u~) so the result is the partonic sigma-hat, directly comparable to
# vibegraph's partonic VEGAS integral.
launch
set lpp1 0
set lpp2 0
set ebeam1 250
set ebeam2 250
set use_syst False
done
